`build/hello.ino.hex` is built from `firmware/hello/hello.ino` for the ATmega328P at 16 MHz.
It links the standard AVR runtime, version 1.8.6. The runtime is free software under the GNU
Lesser General Public License, version 2.1 or any later version, whose text is in
LICENSE-runtime. Its source is the archive at

https://orbefab.com/embedded/sources/avr-1.8.6.tar.bz2

with SHA-256 ff1d17274b5a952f172074bd36c3924336baefded0232e10982f8999c2f7c3b6, served with this
image. It is the archive Arduino publishes at
https://downloads.arduino.cc/cores/staging/avr-1.8.6.tar.bz2. The image was
built with avr-gcc 7.3.0-atmel3.6.1-arduino7 by packages/engine/scripts/sketches.sh in
https://github.com/orbefab/embedded, which pins every archive and relinks the sketch, the
libraries and the runtime, so the image can be rebuilt against a modified runtime. The sketch is
under MIT or Apache-2.0, and those terms permit modifying the image and reverse engineering it to
debug such modifications.

The image also links LiquidCrystal_I2C 2.0.0, under the MIT license, whose notice is in
LICENSE-liquidcrystal-i2c. Its source is the archive at
https://github.com/markub3327/LiquidCrystal_I2C/archive/refs/tags/2.0.0.tar.gz
with SHA-256 627b804fae7b078796817b24f8ac83adc19ddaaeb2c6aaa8e1b3937befe08649.

The image also holds the start-up code of the toolchain's C library, version 2.0.0, under that
library's modified BSD license, whose notice is in LICENSE-libc as the license requires, and
routines of the compiler's support library, under the GCC Runtime Library Exception.

These files and their licences:

`block.jsonc`, `README.md`, `scene.jsonc`, `firmware/NOTICE`, `firmware/hello/hello.ino` and
`tests/hello.test` are under MIT OR Apache-2.0.

`build/hello.ino.hex` links the runtime and LiquidCrystal_I2C, so it is under
LGPL-2.1-or-later and MIT.
`firmware/LICENSE-runtime` is under LGPL-2.1-or-later.
`firmware/LICENSE-liquidcrystal-i2c` is under MIT.
`firmware/LICENSE-libc` is under BSD-3-Clause.
